# Gate step 1375-amye — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS. `tillandsias-plan run` is the portable door that replaces
# timeout(1), setsid(1) and flock(1) in scripts being ported off bash: those
# three differ across GNU, BSD and MSYS, and a Lua decider cannot shell out to
# them. The fixture pins four contracts: --timeout returns 124 without waiting
# the child out; argv stays tokenized; --detach starts a child that leads its
# own session (sid == pid, != caller's — a setpgid-only spawn fails this arm);
# --lock serializes 24 concurrent critical sections and --lock-wait expires
# with 75 without spawning.
#
# Moved here from an inline build.sh step by the coordinator's relay-fix
# (2026-09-30): inline, it ran on every host's --check with no second-regime
# measurement, and its Darwin arm had never executed on a Mac.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the plan run verb's timeout, detach, argv and lock contracts (1375-amye)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-plan-run-verb.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the plan run verb contract failed (1375-amye); see which arm failed above"
STEP_OK="plan run verb: timeout, argv, detach and lock contracts hold"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="tlatoanis-macbook-air 2026-10-08 darwin ok:plan-run-verb:5"
